---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Resources" description="Why AI safety matters, and what NU AI Safety is for.">
  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h1>Resources</h1>

      <p>
        AI systems are becoming more capable and dangerous at a rate faster than we can control
        them. Models are now able to
        <a href="https://openai.com/index/hugging-face-incident-and-the-road-ahead/">hack into other companies</a>,
        <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/research/agentic-misalignment">blackmail users</a>,
        <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.23836">know when they’re being evaluated</a>, and
        even be
        <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/news/disrupting-AI-espionage">used en masse for cyber espionage</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        We want to give Northeastern students the tools and knowledge they need to help align and
        govern AI systems.
      </p>

      <p>
        Some of the people and groups working on this here, described the way each of them
        describes it:
      </p>

      <div class="tabs" data-tabs>
        <section class="tabs__panel" id="landscape-professors" aria-labelledby="landscape-professors-heading" data-tabs-panel>
          <h3 class="tabs__heading" id="landscape-professors-heading" data-tabs-heading>Professors</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <a href="https://baulab.info/">David Bau</a> studies the structure and
              interpretation of deep networks, and leads the
              <a href="https://ndif.us/">National Deep Inference Fabric</a>. He has agreed to
              advise this group and to give guest talks from his lab.
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="https://wyshi.github.io/">Weiyan Shi</a> lists AI safety among her research
              interests, and holds two Open Philanthropy grants on emergent misalignment and on
              evaluating agent safety.
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="https://www.khoury.northeastern.edu/home/alina/">Alina Oprea</a> works on
              adversarial machine learning and trustworthy AI, and on security architectures for
              language model agents.
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="https://www.khoury.northeastern.edu/people/malihe-alikhani/">Malihe Alikhani</a>
              works on AI ethics and is a visiting fellow at the Brookings Institution.
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="https://sinafazelpour.com/">Sina Fazelpour</a>, appointed jointly in Khoury
              and in philosophy, works on the epistemology, ethics and governance of knowledge
              practices in AI-mediated societies, including recent papers on disagreement in AI
              design, evaluation and alignment.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="tabs__panel" id="landscape-organizations" aria-labelledby="landscape-organizations-heading" data-tabs-panel>
          <h3 class="tabs__heading" id="landscape-organizations-heading" data-tabs-heading>Organizations</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <a href="https://ndif.us/">NDIF</a>, described above, calls itself a nationwide
              research computing fabric for transparent and reproducible experiments on the
              largest open AI systems. It is Professor Bau’s NSF-funded project, not something
              this group runs.
            </li>
            <li>
              Northeastern is one of four universities in
              <a href="https://cssh.northeastern.edu/research/projects/center-for-responsible-ai-and-governance/">CRAIG</a>,
              an NSF center on responsible AI and governance.
            </li>
            <li>
              The <a href="https://ai.northeastern.edu/">Institute for Experiential AI</a> names
              responsible AI as one of its four research areas and runs a
              <a href="https://ai.northeastern.edu/responsible-ai-practice">Responsible AI Practice</a>.
            </li>
            <li>
              The <a href="https://cssh.northeastern.edu/ethics/">Ethics Institute</a> lists AI,
              information and data ethics as a primary research area.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>
      </div>

      <script is:inline>
        /* Progressive enhancement. The two panels are server-rendered visible, each under
           its own heading, so with no JavaScript this section reads as two ordinary
           labelled regions with every entry present. This upgrades them to a real tablist:
           roles, aria-selected, aria-controls, roving tabindex, Left/Right/Home/End.
           It runs inline, immediately after the markup it owns, so the panel that is not
           selected is hidden before first paint rather than flashing. */
        (function () {
          var root = document.querySelector('[data-tabs]');
          if (!root) return;
          var panels = Array.prototype.slice.call(root.querySelectorAll('[data-tabs-panel]'));
          if (panels.length < 2) return;

          var list = document.createElement('div');
          list.className = 'tabs__list';
          list.setAttribute('role', 'tablist');
          list.setAttribute('aria-label', 'AI safety work at Northeastern');

          var tabs = panels.map(function (panel) {
            var heading = panel.querySelector('[data-tabs-heading]');
            var tab = document.createElement('button');
            tab.type = 'button';
            tab.className = 'tabs__tab';
            tab.id = panel.id + '-tab';
            tab.setAttribute('role', 'tab');
            tab.setAttribute('aria-controls', panel.id);
            tab.textContent = heading.textContent.trim();
            list.appendChild(tab);

            panel.setAttribute('role', 'tabpanel');
            /* The tab now names the panel, so the visible heading would be read twice. */
            panel.setAttribute('aria-labelledby', tab.id);
            heading.hidden = true;
            return tab;
          });

          function select(i, moveFocus) {
            tabs.forEach(function (tab, j) {
              var on = i === j;
              tab.setAttribute('aria-selected', on ? 'true' : 'false');
              tab.tabIndex = on ? 0 : -1;
              panels[j].hidden = !on;
            });
            if (moveFocus) tabs[i].focus();
          }

          list.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
            var i = tabs.indexOf(e.target.closest('[role="tab"]'));
            if (i > -1) select(i, false);
          });

          list.addEventListener('keydown', function (e) {
            var i = tabs.indexOf(document.activeElement);
            if (i < 0) return;
            var next = null;
            if (e.key === 'ArrowRight') next = (i + 1) % tabs.length;
            else if (e.key === 'ArrowLeft') next = (i - 1 + tabs.length) % tabs.length;
            else if (e.key === 'Home') next = 0;
            else if (e.key === 'End') next = tabs.length - 1;
            if (next === null) return;
            e.preventDefault();
            select(next, true);
          });

          root.insertBefore(list, root.firstChild);
          root.classList.add('tabs--js');
          select(0, false);
        })();
      </script>

      <p>
        None of these people or groups are involved with this group and we are not claiming
        them. They are here because a student deciding where to spend four years should know
        the work is going on around them.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
